From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] edma_v2: port sysctl handlers, vmalloc and callback prototypes to 6.12

Diagnostics:

edma_v2/edma.c:852:19: error: implicit declaration of function 'vzalloc'
edma_v2/edma.c:867:17: error: implicit declaration of function 'vfree'
edma_v2/edma.c:1377:6: error: no previous prototype for
  'edma_configure_mirror_pkt_capture_core'
edma_v2/edma.c:1589:41: error: initialization of
  'int (*)(const struct ctl_table *, int, void *, size_t *, loff_t *)'
  from incompatible pointer type
  'int (*)(struct ctl_table *, int, void *, size_t *, loff_t *)'

Classes:

1. vzalloc/vfree still exist in mainline 6.12 but edma_v2/edma.c relied on
   an indirect include (the vendor kernel's vmalloc.h chain).  Include
   <linux/vmalloc.h> explicitly.  Class: mainline-replaces-API (header
   hygiene only; no behavioural change).

2. edma_configure_mirror_pkt_capture_core() is only used as the callback
   passed to ppe_drv_acl_mirror_core_select_register_cb() in the same file,
   so make it static instead of adding a header entry.
   Class: mainline-replaces-API (Linux 6.10 -Wmissing-prototypes).

3. Linux 6.10 made the sysctl proc_handler take a const struct ctl_table *.
   The seven EDMA handlers (fc enable, queue tail drop, RPS, RPS bitmap,
   hang recovery, vlan append, force crash) are updated in both their
   definitions and their edma.h/edma_cfg_rx.h declarations.

Only the edma_v2 backend is ported here: it is the one SoC=ipq95xx builds.
The edma_v3 backend has the same sysctl-handler pattern plus additional
edma_passthrough_handler/edma_rx_gro_* handlers and a raw ctl_table walk
at edma_v3/edma.c:3191; it is left untouched, and is UNVERIFIED for 6.12
until a target selects it.
diff -ruN a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma.c b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma.c
--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <ppe_drv_port.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/cpumask.h>
+#include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 #include "edma.h"
 #include "edma_cfg_tx.h"
 #include "edma_cfg_rx.h"
@@ -1374,7 +1375,7 @@
  * edma_configure_mirror_pkt_capture_core()
  *	Configure capture core for mirrored packets.
  */
-void edma_configure_mirror_pkt_capture_core(uint8_t core_id, void *app_data)
+static void edma_configure_mirror_pkt_capture_core(uint8_t core_id, void *app_data)
 {
 	edma_cfg_rx_mcast_qid_to_core_mapping(edma_gbl_ctx, core_id);
 }
@@ -2380,7 +2381,7 @@
  * edma_hang_recovery_handler()
  *	to trigger recovery API for EDMA hang
  */
-int edma_hang_recovery_handler(struct ctl_table *table, int write,
+int edma_hang_recovery_handler(const struct ctl_table *table, int write,
                 void __user *buffer, size_t *lenp, loff_t *ppos)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -2402,7 +2403,7 @@
  * edma_vlan_append_handler()
  *	Add VLAN Info.
  */
-int edma_vlan_append_handler(struct ctl_table *table, int write,
+int edma_vlan_append_handler(const struct ctl_table *table, int write,
                 void __user *buffer, size_t *lenp, loff_t *ppos)
 {
 	uint16_t ether_type_0, ether_type_1;
@@ -2581,7 +2582,7 @@
  * edma_force_crash_handler()
  *	Function to trigger crash from EDMA module
  */
-int edma_force_crash_handler(struct ctl_table *table, int write,
+int edma_force_crash_handler(const struct ctl_table *table, int write,
 				void __user *buffer, size_t *lenp, loff_t *ppos)
 {
 	int ret;
diff -ruN a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_cfg_rx.c b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_cfg_rx.c
--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_cfg_rx.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_cfg_rx.c
@@ -1859,7 +1859,7 @@
  * Similarly, whenever the free Rx ring descriptor count crosses the X-ON value,
  * the ring level flow control will be disabled.
